// keystone.aptconf — settings for the image's apt layers
//
// Copied to /etc/apt/apt.conf by every stage that installs packages. apt reads
// that file last, so these settings are the image's final word; update and
// install both take them, with no flag repeated at a call site.
//
// The apt layers fetch from Ubuntu's package mirrors, so a slow or unreachable
// one fails the build. Timeout bounds each connect and each read, so a slow but
// progressing mirror runs to completion; a dead one costs 30s per attempt,
// times the retries.
//
// `apt-get update` exits 0 on a partial index failure and only warns, which
// resurfaces further down as a bogus "Version '*' for <package> was not
// found". Error-Mode "any" makes the failed fetch the error instead.

Acquire::Retries "3";
Acquire::http::Timeout "30";
APT::Update::Error-Mode "any";
